  "label": "Use of Childhood Innocence to Reinforce Racial Stereotypes",
  "description": "The meme uses the visual of a joyful, innocent child to frame a potentially divisive question, which can be interpreted as a harmful stereotype that may reinforce negative perceptions about Black families or parenting structures. The innocence of the child is leveraged to make the question seem more shocking or morally urgent, which is a common tactic in racially charged discourse.",
